    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d223-a2">

                <pb facs="0324" n="250" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg250"/>

                <head>Letter sent to Mr. Harrison</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">United States Consulate</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Toronto</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-07-13"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >July</hi> 13, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir:</hi> I trust you will pardon any seeming
                    importunity on my part when I again ask if Ellis, Dillon, and Carney are to be
                    released. The proof, so clear and full, would, I am confident, satisfy any one
                    of their entire innocence, and I most respectfully ask that the government be
                    requested to discharge them at once. I know their families are suffering, and,
                    in view of the excessive hot weather, it would seem nothing more than justice
                    that they be discharged at once.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, very truly, yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>D. THURSTON, <hi rendition="#italic">United States
                    Consul.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">R. A. Harrison,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Toronto.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
